## 4. Migrations
Apply 0001→0007 in order, once. Corrections go into new files (`0008_…`). Every new tenant table must: carry `company_id`, enable and FORCE RLS,
and call `select app.attach_audit('public.<table>');`. `select * from app.audit_coverage();` must return no rows (the suite checks this).

## 5. Permission-checking conventions for future modules
- Company-level data: `app.has_perm(company_id, 'perm')` — only company-wide roles pass.
- Branch-level data: `app.has_perm(company_id, 'perm', branch_id)` — branch-scoped roles need an assignment. Never pass NULL for branch tables.
- Reads/reports: `app.can_see_branch(company_id, branch_id)` (works for inactive branches).
- New operational documents: `app.can_operate(company_id, 'perm', branch_id)` (requires an ACTIVE branch).
- Posted documents are never deleted: no DELETE policy; correct by reversal documents. Money `numeric(18,4)`, quantities `numeric(18,6)`.
- New SECURITY DEFINER functions: `set search_path = ''`, schema-qualified names, `revoke execute … from public, anon`, grant only what is needed.

## 6. What 0006 changed (from the independent review)
Fail-closed branch scoping; profile visibility limited to active co-members for viewers with `user.view`; invitation flow
(admins invite, invitee accepts); search_path and EXECUTE hardening; removal of the bootstrap GUC flag; inactive branches read-only with
history still readable; audit reason/txid columns, `attach_audit`, `audit_coverage`, audit of permission-matrix changes; `public.user_id_by_email` (service role only).

## 7. Known limitations and pending tasks
- Web app compiled, typechecked and smoke-tested (routing, RTL/LTR, anonymous redirect) but **not run end to end against a real Supabase project**; no browser/UI tests.
- Branch Managers have no user list yet (needs a branch-filtered view). Operational roles (Inventory Controller, Purchasing, Cashier) have no permissions until Phases 2–6 add them.
- Invitation requires working SMTP and the service-role key; users cannot be added any other way by design.
- Company `costing_method` and base currency can be edited now; they must be locked once inventory transactions exist (Phase 3).
- Branch deactivation does not yet check for open/in-transit documents (Phase 3).
- Not built: logo upload (Storage bucket + policies), permissions-matrix viewer, branch comparison, password reset page, MFA, rate limiting beyond Supabase defaults.
- Local tests use a stub of Supabase's `auth` schema and assume the table owner bypasses RLS (true on Supabase's `postgres` role).
- Dependencies were resolved from the registry at build time; run `npm audit` before production.
